From 499f5499643b46f7d37c7689cf8159a39b1a580b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 17:01:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0278 -- fix stale MIDI-set list in the
 unrecognized-MIDI_SOURCE log

Diagnostic-text correctness, no behavior change.

The unrecognized-value LOG_INFO still advertised the pre-nx0262 world:
"Recognized values: wiimidi (default) | orgmid | a path-safe data/<dir>/".
Both halves are now wrong. nx0262 (+ 5605db3 on the SETUP side) made
orgmid2 the shipped default -- unset/empty MIDI_SOURCE resolves to orgmid2
at SoundManager.cpp:812, not wiimidi -- and promoted orgmid1/orgmid2 to
first-class selectable set names (the branch at :860), which the list never
mentioned at all.

This log line is the one place a user lands when they typo a set name, so a
stale list actively misdirects: it tells them the default is wiimidi (it is
not) and hides the two names SETUP actually writes. The list now mirrors the
resolver branches in order -- orgmid2 (default; unset/empty resolves here) |
orgmid1 | wiimidi | orgmid (honors GM_VARIANT v1|v2) | custom drop-in dir.

Behavior is untouched by design. The unrecognized-value fallback stays
wiimidi (_midi_source_dir = "midi"): a fresh install that has not run
`make convert-music` has no data/orgmid2/*.mid, and wiimidi is the set that
ships ready-to-play, so falling back there rather than to the default set is
what keeps a typo from ending in silence. The line documents the registry;
it does not change it.

fmt-arg discipline (nx0263): the rewritten string keeps exactly three '{}'
placeholders in the original order (src, custom-dirs, variant_str) against
the same three arguments -- no arg-count drift.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/sound/SoundManager.cpp | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp b/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
index bbff538b..f5d9e98e 100644
--- a/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
@@ -921,9 +921,11 @@ bool SoundManager::init()
         _midi_source_dir = "midi";
         LOG_INFO("MidiScheduler: unrecognized SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_"
                  "SOURCE value '{}'; falling back to 'wiimidi' (data/midi/). "
-                 "Recognized values: wiimidi (default) | orgmid | a "
-                 "path-safe data/<dir>/ holding >=1 .mid (custom-dirs={}). "
-                 "Variant={} ignored in fallback path.",
+                 "Recognized values: orgmid2 (default; unset/empty resolves "
+                 "here) | orgmid1 | wiimidi | orgmid (honors GM_VARIANT v1|v2 "
+                 "-> data/orgmid1|orgmid2/) | a path-safe data/<dir>/ holding "
+                 ">=1 .mid (custom-dirs={}). Variant={} ignored in fallback "
+                 "path.",
                  src, custom_enabled ? "on" : "off", variant_str);
       }
     }
